<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/honorius" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/honorius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-8">8 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Honorius makes his general Constantius III co-emperor</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honorius">Honorius</a> proclaimed Constantius III, his magister militum and the husband of his sister Galla Placidia, co-emperor in the West. Constantius had put down the usurper Constantine III and recovered much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, but reigned only seven months.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honorius">Honorius</a></div></div></li></ol></section>
